          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.fromBoard" : {
      "comment" : "What the word fromBoard means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Related to-dos. Those board cards that point at a card in main (and branches) by a line or a path in the body and are not finished (done tasks, goals whose status is 完了 or 打ち切り (done or cancelled), and the cards inside them are not shown). It appears in the Properties panel and in card_read"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "関わるやること。main（と branch）のカードを線か本文のパスで指している、ボードのカードのうち済んでいないもの（済んだ task、完了・打ち切りの goal とその中のカードは出さない）。プロパティパネルと card_read に出る"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.ghost" : {
      "comment" : "What the word ghost means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A card ghost. A shortcut placed in a section that points at a card in another section (or at a card ghost) (like an alias in macOS; not a copy). It has its own name; inside the section where it is placed it can be written by that name alone, and from elsewhere as section:name. What it points at (target) is remembered by id and follows renames and moves; if the real card is deleted, it remains as a card ghost pointing at nothing. The section's diagram shows the card it points at in full. Cards in other sections that have no card ghost are gathered into one section ghost per section, and only the parts that are pointed at appear. Something shown only temporarily in the app (a temporary card ghost) does not remain in the project"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "カードゴースト。セクションに置く、ほかのセクションのカード（かカードゴースト）を指すショートカット（macOS のエイリアスのようなもの。コピーではない）。自分の名前を持ち、置いたセクションの中ではその名前だけで書け、ほかからは section:名前 で書ける。指す先（target）は id で覚えて改名・移動に付いて行き、本物が消えると指す先の無いカードゴーストとして残る。セクションの図には指す先のカードが丸ごと出る。カードゴーストの無いほかのセクションのカードは、セクションごとに 1 枚のセクションゴーストにまとまり、指されている所だけが出る。画面で一時的に出すだけのもの（一時カードゴースト）はプロジェクトに残らない"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.goal" : {
      "comment" : "What the word goal means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A goal. A container card that has the fields status (the state), priority, due (the due date), workBranch (the branch to work in) and MR, and a body (body); goals and tasks are placed inside it. The inner order is the order of work for tasks. It is placed in a goals section or a free section of the Project Board"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "目標。status（状態）・priority（優先度）・due（期限）・workBranch（作業する branch）・MR の欄と、本文（body）を持つ入れ物のカードで、中に goal と task を置く。中の並びが task の作業の順。プロジェクトボードの goals のセクションとフリーセクションに置く"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.html" : {
      "comment" : "What the word html means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "An HTML page. Its body (body) is HTML (CSS too); on a diagram the card draws it laid out at its box's width and cut at the box. Scripts, loading from outside and form submission do not work (sb-nav:<path> links open in the app, http and https in the browser). Placed in document, free and UI sections, and can be resized. When exported, one card is one file (.html, with the same protection at its head)"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "HTML のページ。本文（body）に HTML（CSS も）を書き、図の上ではカードの箱の幅で組んで箱で切って描く。スクリプト・外の読み込み・フォームの送信は動かない（sb-nav:<パス> のリンクはアプリの中で、http・https はブラウザで開く）。ドキュメント・フリー・UI のセクションに置き、大きさを変えられる。エクスポートすると 1 枚が 1 ファイル（.html。頭に同じ守りを書く）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.in" : {
      "comment" : "What the word in means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The container that a card inside a container card (flow, goal; the holds of the kind definition lists the kinds that can be put inside) is in. The path of an inner card is the container's path followed by its name (Behavior:Checkout.review, Goals:Launch.Design). Move a card to another container with in of card_update"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "入れ物のカード（flow・goal。種類の定義の holds に中に置ける種類がある）の中のカードが入っている入れ物。中のカードのパスは入れ物のパスに名前を続ける（Behavior:Checkout.review・Goals:Launch.Design）。card_update の in で入れ物を移す"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.initiator" : {
      "comment" : "What the word initiator means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The side that makes the call: self / peer (separate from the direction of the data)"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "呼びに行く側: self / peer（データの向きとは別）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.instance" : {
      "comment" : "What the word instance means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Data. An example (instance) of an entity or value (an actual value with a shape). It is placed in a Definition section (definition; Definitions at a new project's root) or a free section. The shape is the of line (in MCP, the shape's path in the value key of), and the values are held in data. The diagram and the editor line up a type tag and a value for each field of the shape. The path of one value is Data:first.status (elements of an array are Data:first.lines[0] and Data:first.lines[sku=A-1]). It appears in examples of the shape's JSON Schema and in the table of a card row of a document"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "データ。entity・value の実例（形を持つ実際の値）。定義のセクション（definition。新しいプロジェクトでは根の Definitions）とフリーセクションに置く。形は線 shapeOf（MCP は value のキー of に形のパス）、値は data に持つ。図とエディタは形のフィールドごとに型の札と値を並べる。値 1 つのパスは Data:first.status（並びの要素は Data:first.lines[0]・Data:first.lines[sku=A-1]）。形の JSON Schema の examples と、文書の card の行の表に出る"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.join" : {
      "comment" : "What the word join means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A join. With two or more next lines, it waits until the destinations that split up have all arrived (join: all / any / first, partial: fail / continue)"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "合流。next の線を 2 本以上にして分かれた行き先がそろうのを待つ（join: all / any / first、partial: fail / continue）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.line" : {
      "comment" : "What the word line means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The kind of a line. Built-in ones (embed, points, link, holds, shapeOf, rules, implementedBy, mentions, and the lines of flow nodes: next, condition, else, onError, onTimeout, runs, awaits, reads, writes, partner, key) and ones the project defines. The meaning (base of the definition) is embed (the type becomes the partner), designate (the type does not change and the partner is pointed at), or link (unrelated to the type). Read them with kind_list and kind_read, and define them with kind_create and kind_update"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "線の種類。組み込み（embed・points・link・holds・shapeOf・rules・implementedBy・mentions と、flow のノードの線 next・condition・else・onError・onTimeout・runs・awaits・reads・writes・partner・key）とプロジェクトが定義するもの。意味（定義の base）は embed（型が相手になる）・designate（型は変わらず相手を指す）・link（型に関係しない）。kind_list・kind_read で読み、kind_create・kind_update で定義する"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "term.main" : {
      "comment" : "What the word main means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The tree that represents the current implementation. There is one per project"
