    "term.mock" : {
      "comment" : "What the word mock means, in the glossary and the help of the screen.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A mock. One HTML page built from a UI section's parts, each where it is placed and as big as it is placed (a frame holds the mock of the UI section it points at; note cards are not drawn; scripts do not run). In MCP, read it with section_read as: mock (html, width, height, parts, frames), with each part's own page (faces) added by faces: true, and as a picture with as: picture. The app's section map draws the parts from their own pages. When exported, each UI section is one .html"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "モック。UI のセクションの部品を、置いた所に置いた大きさで組み上げた 1 枚の HTML のページ（はめ込みには指す先の UI のセクションのモックが入る。note のカードは描かない。スクリプトは動かない）。MCP は section_read の as: mock（html・width・height・parts・frames）で読み、faces: true で部品ごとのページ（faces）も添え、as: picture で絵。画面のセクションマップは部品ごとのページで部品を描く。エクスポートすると UI のセクションごとに 1 枚の .html"
          }
        }
      }
    },
